Finding: {"title":"Client-side publish gates (conflicts, review checklist, override reason) have no server-side re-verification","severity":"MEDIUM","area":"Defense-in-depth / business-rule enforcement","files":["src/components/features/mvp-v2/pages/ai-schedule-sandbox.tsx","src/server/routes/routes-ai-schedule.ts"],"detail":"handlePublishIntent (ai-schedule-sandbox.tsx:2948-2996) blocks publish client-side when `conflicts.length > 0`, the review checklist isn't complete, or a required override reason is empty. None of these are re-checked by POST /drafts/:draftId/publish or /publish-selected server-side — those endpoints only check `requireAdmin()` and blindly insert whatever events are in the draft's `scheduleEvents` payload, including any `_conflict` events.","impact":"Any direct API call (bypassing the UI — a compromised admin session, a scripted call, or a future UI bug) can publish conflicting/unreviewed events straight to the live schedule with no server-side guard.","recommendation":"At minimum, have /publish and /publish-selected re-run an overlap check against `schedule_events` for the events being inserted (similar to the existing-events occupancy logic already implemented in runScheduleSolver) and reject/flag conflicting ones rather than trusting client-computed conflict state.","confidence":"medium"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

